# Every ignore rule this repository depends on lives in this file. That is a rule, not an
# observation: git consults three sources and a clone receives only this one. The other two are
# `.git/info/exclude`, which git creates fresh in every clone, and the machine's global excludes
# file, which is somebody's home directory - neither is written here, because this repository
# publishes. Until 2026-09-02 both rules covering `.claude/` came from those two, so on one
# machine a local settings file never appeared as untracked while on every other machine
# `git add -A` would have staged it into a public repository (PR-15, PR-122). A rule that
# protects only its author is not protection.

# Local scratch — never published. `control/` and `dist/` are **conventional, not observed**:
# neither has appeared in any commit of this repository, and `check_all.py`'s `tracked()`
# docstring cites both as worked examples of what is machine-local by design. Nothing here looks
# at what this file hides - `refcheck.py` reads it only to skip - and that is deliberate rather
# than a gap: an ignored surface differs on every clone, so a checker over it would fail
# differently for every adopter (PR-123).
control/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Live handoff state is machine-local; the config is not
.handoff/HANDOFF.md
.handoff/processed_*

# Machine state under `.claude/`, named one line at a time rather than by the directory.
# `.claude/` itself is deliberately NOT ignored: whether this repository should track a rule
# file at all is T-295's decision, and a wholesale rule would take that decision quietly -
# which is how the probe below came to be published before anyone chose. The worktrees line
# was `.git/info/exclude`'s until 2026-09-02 and so reached no clone at all.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# A test instrument, not a rule: T-288's probe, which T-295 deletes when it takes the
# reading. `git add -A` published this one before anyone chose; hence the line.
.claude/rules/t-288-probe.md

# Corpus knowledgebase — full-fidelity extraction of the owner's private notes.
# Local-only by construction: it contains client and personal data and must never publish.
.kb/
.assets-cache/

# Presenter builds. A second artifact from the same specification, carrying the speaker notes
# DS-088 keeps out of a shipped deck (T-211 section 3, T-213). It is generated beside the deck
# because that is where a presenter wants it, and ignored here because it must never be committed:
# `check_all.py` fails any tracked `.html` it has no entry for, so a committed one would go red -
# correctly, and one release later than this line does.
*-presenter.html

# Printed output. The repository keeps the script and the numbers, never the artefact (R6),
# and a printed PDF also carries whatever the print dialog put in its header.
examples/*.pdf
